once celebrated as a Liberation party  that fought against racial segregation  in recent years South Africa's governing  African National Congress has been  riddled by corruption and criticism  it's the party of respected Global and  African leaders such as Oliver tumbo and  Nobel Peace Prize Laureate Nelson  Mandela  28 years into democracy the anc's facing  increasing condemnation for poor  leadership and governance  since Mandela subsequent presidents Tabo  and Becky and Jacob Zuma were recalled  or forced to resign current president  Sil ramaphosa is facing similar pressure  in a scandal involving the theft of  hundreds of thousands of dollars from  his game farm the anc's reputation for  many is in tatters kleptocracy nepotism  card rate deployment from the very  beginning of the ANC government which  then became a norm within the party and  within the higher echelons of government  so even when people are found to have  sallied their their their their their  their record as it were they still  continue to be deployed as members of  the ANC and as trusted members of the  ANC and that's what's led to rampant  corruption a poorly performing economy  record high unemployment and energy  crisis and a multitude of fraud scams  have frustrated South Africans the party  won the first Democratic elections in  1994 with a 60 two percent majority that  dropped to 57 in the last polls support  for the anc's been in Decline for years  some voters have protested against the  ANC by staying away from the polls  others have abandoned the governing  party and voted for the opposition the  Democratic Alliance and economic freedom  fighters dominate opposition voices  while their combined support of almost a  third of Voters can't be ignored an ANC  parliamentary majority is often  protected its embattled leaders  the ANC needed money and the people  who supported the ANC saw money as being  something that they could get their  hands on so the solution was  you could relatively 